<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115349" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψάμμος</span></b> , ἡ, but in
			<i><span class="en">
			Archim.
			<u>Aren.</u>
			1.1
		</span></i>, al., always ὁ:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sand,</i> used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψάμαθος</span> only in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.243
			</span></i>, later very freq., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.71
			</span></i>, etc.: pl., <i>grains of sand,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἀπ᾽ ἀλλήλων ἐσκεδασμέναι ψάμμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.130
				</span></i>
			: prov., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψάμμος ἀριθμὸν περιπέφευγεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					2.98
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶδα δ᾽ ἐγὼ ψάμμου τ᾽
			ἀριθμόν</span> Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.47
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ ψάμμου σχοινίον
			πλέκειν,</span> of labour in vain, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				2.309J.
			</span></i>; of something worthless, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Wi.</u>
				7.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i> Chr.<i><span class="en">
				77
			</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				8.30
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψάμμου ἄξιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Oenom.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				5.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metallic ore
			used by alchemists, in pl., Olymp.Alch.<i><span class="en">
				p.106B.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Zos.Alch.
				p.239
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ψ.</span> the <i>sandy desert</i> of
			Libya, the <i>sand,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.173
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλείστης ψάμμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					666.27
				</span></i>
			 (Egypt, <span class="entity">i A. D.</span>). (Prob. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ψαφ-μος,</span> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψαφαρός,
				ψῆφος,</span> Lat. <i>sabulum.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
